      spring: "Changeable and greening — afternoons rising from about 12°C in March to 23°C by late May, with frosty mornings into April, frequent showers, and redbud and dogwood flowering on the hillsides. Late snow is possible in March, and thunderstorms arrive by May.",
      summer: "Warm, humid and green — afternoons near 28°C, nights around 16°C, and frequent afternoon thunderstorms building over the hills. The forested ridges keep the city lush, and the rail-trail along the river is busy with walkers and cyclists. Valley fog returns at dawn on calm, muggy mornings.",
      autumn: "Mild and colourful — September afternoons near 25°C easing to about 12°C by November, morning fog in the river valley burning off to clear, crisp days, and the hills turning red and gold in October, just in time for football weekends.",
